ich allows  you to move funds between accounts to  use Fiat to buy crypto vice versa  etc what is the sort of security  infrastructure of that and ultimately  who is holding the crypto when people  are using your platform so we are not  holding money or crypto I mean Peter or  crypto we're only providing an access to  user account for example if you have it  an account with finance we would take  the API key and access your account  advance through our dashboard so you  would basically see the balance but the  money the crypto is going to be at the  exchange same goes with the banking  accounts if you have euros we would  access the balance account information  and will basically see the numbers but  we won't keep the money and same goes  with transaction initiation if we can  initiate transaction from your bank  account to finance but we won't  the money will go straight from your  bank account to finance without we won't  touch the money like they will go  straight so what we basically what  access we have we have access to your  information to information about the  account balance but we don't store it  basically we show it to you and we have  intent encryption and in order to login  into the system you need to do to a fee  or certification and each time you do it  you basically kind of send the  permission to access to API keys to  access their API keys so now we store  very little of information and it's  basically not vulnerable one of the main  features of the Oracle platform is this  marketplace that exists for apps what is  talked to us a little bit about that  what are the types of apps that will be  available how will they interact with  platform so marketplace is something  it's one more step towards user mass  adoption let's say that because for now  we see a lot of different very cool  projects that are doing different  financial services on blockchain crypto  lending and etc but most of the time in  order to use them or when they will  deliver the product in order to use it  you will need to have their token  meaning that if you use like 5 10 20  different services you need always to  keep these 10 tokens 10 different tokens  in your wallet go around different  exchanges buy them so we don't we think  this is not really convenient this is  why we created a marketplace where we  have all these different crypto  financial services and we integrate  their token without token using banker  liquidity protocol so when you go to the  marketplace you just need one token Orca  token to access all these services and  these services are salt lending a blend  SDK and more and more and more services  that you can also buy trading algorithms  that will that you will attach to your  exchange API and they will trade for you  like follow trend arbitrage algorithms  because we can see different exchanges  different accounts there and we can do  arbitrage also not we but the algorithms  and this is the why we see a clear need  for marketplace because what we're doing  here we're trying to solve certain  problems to tackle certain challenges  and the marketplaces act is for sure  solving ones so where does the token  come into all this what does it do and  and what what utility does it have so  the main utility as I mentioned it has  because you can access the the apps on  the marketplace you can access them like  for example if there is let's say I  don't know F land and you want to use  you need land  tokens we would integrate bank through  bankroll equality protocol would  integrate land tokens with Orca tokens  and we would just do the swap for you so  you would paid with Orca tokens but we  would do the exchange and you would be  able to use the service what about the  ICO what's the sort of status of the ICO  at this point so we're doing a private  sale currently it's going pretty well we  almost closed it I think we'll close it  in two weeks maybe in ten days and from  then we'll announce that the date of the  public sale s